-- title:
--   Regularity of the fibre at the Gauss-component generic point
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) at level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; that is, $K$ is generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of that function field. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in the maximal ideal of $A$, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, made an $A$-algebra over $K$ compatibly with $A \to L \to K$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ satisfying: $f \in W_0$ if and only if there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f \cdot \mathrm{ofPowerSeries}(y) = \mathrm{ofPowerSeries}(x)$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ (the Gauss valuation ring of $A$-integral $q$-expansions). Write $\mathfrak X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$ along the middle chart. Let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak X$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak X$ obtained by pulling back $\varpi \in A$ along [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258), and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X, z}$. Assume further that $z$ is the image under the canonical morphism from the finite chart $\mathrm{Spec}$ of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142) of a point $y$ whose prime ideal is not maximal, and that every element $b$ of that chart algebra whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in the prime of $y$. Then the quotient of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X, z}$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   At the generic point of the component of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model cut out by the Gauss valuation ring of $A$-integral $q$-expansions, the uniformiser $\varpi$ generates the maximal ideal up to radical in the strong sense that the fibre ring is regular; equivalently, this component of the special fibre occurs with multiplicity one, the ramification index of the Gauss valuation over $A$ being one. It feeds the construction of an open subscheme of the model that is smooth over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_opens_smooth_comp_toBase_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_of_forall_not_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_xH_of_isAlgebraic`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_opens_smooth_comp_toBase_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_of_forall_not_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_xH_of_isAlgebraic).
